flowchart TB
    CP["Committee checkpoint<br/>pre+post state-root · data commitment · committee VRF-sigs"]
    subgraph V1["v1 — committee sig-threshold trust (ships first; unblocks #259)"]
        direction TB
        T1["gl0 + consumers verify<br/>more than 2/3 committee VRF-sigs over checkpoint bytes"]
        T2["deterministic admit then trust claimed state<br/>(NO re-execution by non-committee)"]
        T1 --> T2
    end
    CP --> T1
    NOTE1["SAFE ONLY IF per-bucket honest-majority holds.<br/>Without the v2 backstop, v1 needs Algorand-sized committees;<br/>a small per-bucket committee is unsafe (cross-shard CQ-collapse)."]
    V1 -.-> NOTE1
    subgraph V2["v2 — availability + fraud-proof + slashing (hardens trust; lets committees shrink)"]
        direction TB
        DA["DA gate (Polkadot): erasure-code data,<br/>block finality until at least 1/3+1 hold a chunk"]
        AP["approval-checkers (ELVES): VRF-sampled AFTER signing,<br/>re-execute a random subset, escalate on no-show"]
        DIS["disputes to 2/3 supermajority +<br/>asymmetric slashing: ~100% false-valid, ~0% honest dissent + rollback"]
        DA --> AP --> DIS
    end
    T2 --> DA
    ALT["ALTERNATIVE end-state (NEAR): ship a STATE WITNESS with the checkpoint<br/>so verifiers re-execute over the witness = validity-before-inclusion.<br/>No challenge window, no rollback. Fits MPT-primary subtree-stub."]
    V2 -.->|or| ALT
